      {
        "id": 194610,
        "name": "Kratos13",
        "username": "Kratos13",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/65b543/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-04-06T05:01:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Well, a simplified example would be if there was exactly one environment card you wanted to avoid. &nbsp;In a normal game, after 15 rounds there is a 100% chance that you will have encountered that card (barring any other deck discarding effects). &nbsp;If you used RC Wraith's power every single turn, after 7 rounds there's approx 50% that you dodged that card. &nbsp;After the reshuffle and another 8 rounds there is another approx 50% you dodged that card again. &nbsp;So in this case there's a 25% chance you got to avoid the card after 15 rounds as opposed to the base case of 0%. &nbsp;So it's a relatively minor improvement and unless it's 3 player or Akash, most games don't last 15 rounds and it costs Wraith 15 power uses. &nbsp;Also consider after 7 rounds, it's 50% chance you dodged the card, but in the base case, it's also 50% chance that that card hasn't shown up yet. &nbsp;So for shorter games there's basically no improvement.</p><p>But consider looking for exactly one good card. &nbsp;RC Wraith essentially goes through the deck at double speed, meaning you should be able to get your card 1-7 rounds sooner. &nbsp;For short games that may only last 5-7 rounds that's a great boon.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
