        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"mwc146\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n mwc146:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In my experience, Rook City Wraith excels most in Rook City, where you'll want to avoid&nbsp;<em>most</em>&nbsp;of the cards, and popping them straight into the trash avoids the harsher destroy conditions, like those cards that play from the villain deck when they're destroyed.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Not to mention that she makes it far more likely that you get to see the two cards in the Rook City deck you actually <em>do</em> want to see <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
