      {
        "id": 194614,
        "name": "deddragon",
        "username": "deddragon",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/deddragon/{size}/2335_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-04-06T23:22:11.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Barely Minted. I think one more round would have done me in as all characters were at 4 or less except Absolute Zero (who healed a little extra the last round due to the 2nd Frosthound.)</p>\n<p>I went with a straight-up beat-down, taking advantage of the Panzer Buster to drive hard after Voss.  I completely ignored all other targets, ending with 8 minions in play but no Ships or Translocators.</p>\n<p>I did make two mistakes that might have made things a little less close.</p>\n<p>First, I messed up Tachyon’s card play order once. When Pushing the Limits, I really needed to deal with the Traffic Pileup BEFORE playing Fleet of Foot.</p>\n<p>Second, for some reason I was thinking start of turn effects resolved in the order used, thus meaning I could take advantage of Panzer Buster with Gattling Gun. Not the case, as it’s the order the cards entered play, and clearly Bunker was in play prior to his first turn.</p>\n<p>Ah well. Minty first Ultimate, that’s all that matters to me <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=9\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\"></p>",
        "post_number": 28,
